["How blessed and wonderful, beloved, are the gifts of God! Life in immortality, splendor in righteousness, truth with boldness, faith with confidence, self-control with holiness: all these already lie within our understanding. What, then, is being prepared for those who endure? The all-holy Creator and Father of the ages himself knows how great and how beautiful those things are. So let us strive to be found among those who endure, that we may share in the gifts he has promised.", "And how shall this be, beloved? It will be if our mind is set faithfully on God; if we seek what pleases him and what he accepts; if we carry out what fits his blameless will and follow the way of truth, casting away from us all wrongdoing and wickedness, greed, quarrels, malice and deceit, gossip and slander, hatred of God, pride and boasting, empty glory and want of hospitality. For those who do these things are hateful to God, and not only those who do them, but those who approve of them as well.", "For the Scripture says: “But to the sinner God said: ‘What right have you to recite my statutes, or to take my covenant on your lips? You hated instruction and threw my words behind you. When you saw a thief, you ran along with him, and you threw in your lot with adulterers. Your mouth overflowed with evil, and your tongue wove deceit. You sat and slandered your brother, and laid a stumbling block before your own mother's son. You did these things, and I kept silent; you thought, lawless one, that I would be like you. I will rebuke you and set you before your own face. Consider this, you who forget God, lest he seize you like a lion, with no one to rescue you. A sacrifice of praise will glorify me, and there is the way by which I will show him the salvation of God’” (Psalm 50:16-23)."]